For controller users who have modified their Fallout4Prefs.ini uPipboyTargetHeight and uPipboyTargetWidth to double the resolution size of the Pipboy screen and found that the virtual mouse cursor on the map was locked to the top left quadrant I believe I have found a fix.

In addition to doubling the values for the above you need to double the values that setup the boundaries for the virtual cursor in Fallout4Custom.ini.

So both .ini files should have the following entries:

Fallout4Prefs.ini

[Display]
uPipboyTargetHeight=1400
uPipboyTargetWidth=1752

Fallout4Custom.ini

[Pipboy]
uPipboyConstraintWidth=1450
uPipboyConstraintWidth_PowerArmor=1110
uPipboyConstraintHeight=1020
uPipboyConstraintHeight_PowerArmor=760
uPipboyConstraintTLX_PowerArmor=320
uPipboyConstraintTLX=150
uPipboyConstraintTLY=190
uPipboyConstraintTLY_PowerArmor=320


If you want to revert to defaults here are the DEFAULT values:
Fallout4Prefs.ini

[Display]
uPipboyTargetHeight=700
uPipboyTargetWidth=876

Fallout4Custom.ini

[Pipboy]
uPipboyConstraintWidth=725
uPipboyConstraintWidth_PowerArmor=555
uPipboyConstraintHeight=510
uPipboyConstraintHeight_PowerArmor=380
uPipboyConstraintTLX_PowerArmor=160
uPipboyConstraintTLX=75
uPipboyConstraintTLY=95
uPipboyConstraintTLY_PowerArmor=160
